# 046 · Web search for research mode

**Status:** `VERIFIED` · **Version:** [v0.6.0](../../roadmap.md#v060)

## What

A search provider in Providers, used by research workers and, where the owner allows it, by advisors. Today research follows seed links only.

## Why

Research mode cannot build a sourced corpus without search.

## Done when

- [x] A research campaign finds and cites sources through the provider. (Through an MCP server, goal [068](068-mcp-servers-for-agents.goal): a research campaign's workers searched the web with a search and browsing server's tools and recorded verified claims from what they found, beyond their starting links.)

## Decisions

- 2026-10-23, lead, on the owner's question ("I feel like the research already gets our MCP so it can do web search right?"): web search reaches research workers, and advisors where a campaign allows it, as an MCP server the campaign names ([068](068-mcp-servers-for-agents.goal)), not as a search provider of its own in Providers. That meets this goal, so no search provider is built.

## Open questions

None.

## Progress

- 2026-10-19: Goal written from the roadmap.
- 2026-10-23: Met by goal 068's MCP servers. The pages say how research searches the web (Campaign modes; Known limits, where the limit now reads that research searches only through an MCP server). Verified.

